     (8.5.5+) Deferrable work
     To schedule non-urgent work with a delay (e.g., background cleanup tasks), components should get java.util.concurrent.ScheduledExecutorService from the service registry with deferrable=true. This service has lower service.ranking (lower precedence) than the non-deferrable ScheduledExecutorService, but components can explicitly request the deferrable=false. This is similar to the tWAS AlarmManager.createDeferrable API.
